note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note gpu/nvidia/driver/card.om: which GPU the driver client opens, and the class list it hands to amp_runtime.
note Omega form of CUDApp nvrm/nvrm.c card_index and the marshalling half of select_classes (84b524ca).
note Needs OM-2 (unsized views): compose after an om2 part; gpu/nvidia/driver/parts.txt lists the order.
note Card table: the bytes NV_ESC_CARD_INFO fills, records of 72 bytes (nv_ioctl_card_info_t of NVIDIA open
note 580.173.02): valid u8 at 0, PCI domain u32 LE at 4, bus u8 at 8, slot u8 at 9, function u8 at 10. The C
note walks 64 records; here the record count is the table length divided by 72, so a caller hands 64.

note value of one lowercase hex digit, or 16 when c is not one ("%x" output is lowercase)
fn drv_hexd c ulong to ulong
if and ge c 48 le c 57
ret sub c 48
end
if and ge c 97 le c 102
ret sub c 87
end
ret 16
end

note the hex digits b[s, s + n) as one number, or 2^64 - 1 when one of them is not a lowercase hex digit
fn drv_hexn b view uchar * s ulong n ulong to ulong
v = ulong 0
for i ulong n bound 8
d = drv_hexd ulong get b add s i
if gt d 15
ret 18446744073709551615
end
v = add shl v 4 d
end
ret v
end

note A BDF the C accepts: sscanf "%x:%x:%x.%x%c" reads exactly four fields, domain <= 0xffff, bus <= 0xff,
note slot <= 0x1f, function <= 7, and the text equals its own "%04x:%02x:%02x.%x". That is exactly
note dddd:bb:ss.f in lowercase hex, 12 bytes. o gets domain, bus, slot, function. False refuses it.
fn drv_bdf b view uchar * o edit ulong 4 to bool
if ne len b 12
ret false
end
if or ne get b 4 58 or ne get b 7 58 ne get b 10 46
ret false
end
d = drv_hexn b 0 4
u = drv_hexn b 5 2
s = drv_hexn b 8 2
f = drv_hexn b 11 1
if or gt d 65535 or gt u 255 or gt s 31 gt f 7
ret false
end
put o 0 d
put o 1 u
put o 2 s
put o 3 f
ret true
end

note little-endian u32 at byte p of the card table
fn drv_u32 c view uchar * p ulong to ulong
a = ulong get c p
b = shl ulong get c add p 1 8
x = shl ulong get c add p 2 16
y = shl ulong get c add p 3 24
ret or or a b or x y
end

note card_index: with has false, the first valid card; with has true, the first valid card whose PCI address
note is the BDF in b (refused BDF: none). Returns the card index plus one, 0 when there is none.
fn drv_card c view uchar * has bool b view uchar * to ulong
o = new ulong 4 0
n = div len c 72
if has
if not drv_bdf b o
ret 0
end
end
for i ulong n bound 9223372036854775807
p = mul i 72
if ne get c p 0
if not has
ret add i 1
end
if drv_at c p o
ret add i 1
end
end
end
ret 0
end

note the card record at byte p has the PCI address o[0..3]
fn drv_at c view uchar * p ulong o view ulong 4 to bool
if ne drv_u32 c add p 4 get o 0
ret false
end
if ne ulong get c add p 8 get o 1
ret false
end
if ne ulong get c add p 9 get o 2
ret false
end
ret eq ulong get c add p 10 get o 3
end

note select_classes marshalling: the amp_runtime class-set request m for SM sm and PCI vendor:device. Bit k of
note m[10] says the vendor list holds Ampere class m[4 + k] (compute B, GPFIFO A, Volta usermode A); bit k of
note m[11] says it holds Blackwell class m[7 + k] (compute B, channel GPFIFO A, Hopper usermode A).
fn drv_marshal sm ulong vendor ulong device ulong cls view uint * m edit ulong 16 to void
for z ulong 16
put m z 0
end
put m 0 1
put m 1 sm
put m 2 0x806
put m 3 0xc01
put m 4 0xc7c0
put m 5 0xc56f
put m 6 0xc361
put m 7 0xcec0
put m 8 0xc96f
put m 9 0xc661
put m 12 0xa04
put m 13 vendor
put m 14 device
for i ulong len cls bound 9223372036854775807
v = ulong get cls i
for k ulong 3
if eq v get m add 4 k
put m 10 or get m 10 shl ulong 1 k
end
if eq v get m add 7 k
put m 11 or get m 11 shl ulong 1 k
end
end
end
end

note select_classes: s gets target SM, discrete, compute, GPFIFO and usermode class; false is the C refusal
note "unsupported SM 0x%x or missing target classes" (s is then all zero).
fn drv_select sm ulong vendor ulong device ulong cls view uint * s edit ulong 5 to bool
m = new ulong 16 0
q = new ulong 64 0
drv_marshal sm vendor device cls m
for z ulong 5
put s z 0
end
if ne amp_runtime m q 1
ret false
end
for z ulong 5
put s z get q z
end
ret true
end

note nvrm_retire and nvrm_chan_retire (nvrm/nvrm.c): the channel's retired GPFIFO count after the caller reports
note completion up to up. It moves only when up lies in [rt, pt] counted forward from rt with u32 wrap:
note (up - rt) <= (pt - rt). For u32 inputs the 64-bit differences order exactly as the 32-bit ones do (a
note difference that wraps is above every one that does not, in both widths), so no mask is needed.
fn drv_retire rt ulong pt ulong up ulong to ulong
if le sub up rt sub pt rt
ret up
end
ret rt
end
